	(text "Generate HSync and VSync\nGenerate Blank\n\nVSync starts at Y reset\nVSync ends at row 31\n\nHSync start at column 410\nHSync ends at column 437\n\nBlank is VSync or start at Column 402\nBlank is VSync or ends at X reset\n\nGenerate Output Control Multiplexer\n\nOutput Multiplex Control (3 bit)\nUsing LS148 priority multiplexer\n\n0 = Tile\n1 = Bitmap\n2 = External\n3 = Sprite\n4 = Border\n5 = Blank\n6 = VSync\n7 = HSync"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.732 14.986 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ff114d87-0ae5-469c-a63e-ba1026c7fb9e")
	)
	(text_box "Frame Timing module generates the sync and porch phases of the NTSC and PAL signal format\nFor simplicity the horizontal count ignores the lowest bit so \"counts\" here are half that of the position counters module\n\nThe vertical sync starts with a vertical reset pulse and ends after 32 rows\n\nThe porch starts at X position 402 and ends with a horizontal reset pulse\n\nThe horizontal sync sits roughly in the middle of the porch, starting at 410 and ending at 438\n\nThe result of the horizontal count is a horizontal sync pulse duration of 4us and a porch duration of 8us\nAs noted in the PositionCounters module, if the clock input is changed the start/end counts must be recalculated\n\nAdditionally, the module generates an encoded signal to select the correct video source, this is vital to ensure the correct output levels during sync and porch (blank), it also draws on the ViewPort module timing signals to select an output for the border\n\nOther select signals are provided by their modules but the encoder uses a priority mechanism to ensure that nothing can override Sync and Porch phases and as such guarantees the frame timing remains stable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 114.3 0)
		(size 66.04 62.23)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6e8744e6-de2b-494c-9972-b21659dc9792")
	)
